{"title":"2008 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/0/6e00bb0b21c77566dd62c55ffe79136b54b24953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JLMR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c512375b7ce6770c119fdd77e5907b2d657505fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JKQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> are rectangles. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cdb130eb87ba80e6c7265312233fdf7ad65eba0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JR = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/b/40b17146a45dd02629c739315cc7c10a4783905e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RQ = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/658fdc581f5c4595251e26c942750999c5762ce8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JL = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>What is the area of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/c/90c03dcb5acbc259eef5e5da95c6027341b37822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KLMQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34e727ea4526179ea48da709f1fd66900bc90f19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 6 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 16 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 10 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 15 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"424\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since opposite sides in a rectangle are equal, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/a/06a1e5e6affa1bc39a5f04041279f35555199e1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MR = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"69\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/9/649a393251279c7b170d1daae253d706b7dc4214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KQ = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859356a4f63456a4acbb1f2b191982b4aa400279.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"33\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/0/8908a2be2692d4eb840757cd862a1fd76a024398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"16\" /> sum up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/7/77706943210a5dbe1ee238f65c0cd2e9bb0b7050.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MR$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/a/1ca4ae965fbf79d1a18e2522d3f2533c15cb4158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MQ = MR - RQ = 8 - 3 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"242\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The area of a rectangle is equal to its length multiplied by its height, so the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/c/90c03dcb5acbc259eef5e5da95c6027341b37822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KLMQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/e/dae2bfd3d5a54e4c853891ca1c7a6d8a61175e65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 5 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"131\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The combined areas of rectangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/c/90c03dcb5acbc259eef5e5da95c6027341b37822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KLMQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c512375b7ce6770c119fdd77e5907b2d657505fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JKQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> is the area of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/0/6e00bb0b21c77566dd62c55ffe79136b54b24953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JLMR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. The area of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c512375b7ce6770c119fdd77e5907b2d657505fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JKQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/6/7665cc4223d31e60fba93de9e8e901b3bd737b3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 3 = 6$\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" /> and the area of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/0/6e00bb0b21c77566dd62c55ffe79136b54b24953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JLMR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/2/942406ff49f6d27f36ffe86f13b57601b402821c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 8 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The area of rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/c/90c03dcb5acbc259eef5e5da95c6027341b37822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KLMQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/e/39e061b1885bc6de93bda77c1f48dbb90e1c8a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 - 6 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"2008 CEMC Pascal\">2008 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2008 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2008 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2008 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Probl